# Tabs

Tabs show one of several related sections in the same view.

These are civica.uk reference implementations for component authors. They do not replace native Home Assistant behaviour or demonstrate a connection to a live home.

## When to use it

Use them for frequent users who need to switch quickly between clearly named information groups. Put the most useful section first and keep each panel small enough to load promptly.

## When not to use it

Do not use tabs as the application’s main route navigation, for a sequential setup process, or when people need to compare both panels side by side. Do not hide urgent device conditions in an unselected tab.

## Home Assistant adaptation

A device reference might separate current details from its event history. Preserve the selected tab during unrelated sensor updates and avoid refetching or resetting the user’s position unnecessarily. An empty panel should explain why it has no values rather than disabling its tab.

## Accessibility and behaviour

Use a proven tab implementation with tablist, tab and tabpanel relationships, roving focus and arrow-key navigation. The GOV.UK reference progressively becomes a contents list and stacked sections on small screens or without enhancement.

